  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <h1>Best Ecommerce Platforms in 2026</h1>
      <div class="meta">Updated July 2026 · Ranked 4 platforms · Ecommerce Pillar</div>

      <p>Choosing the right ecommerce platform decides how fast you launch, how much you pay in fees, and whether your store can scale when orders grow. Shopify, WooCommerce, BigCommerce, and Squarespace are the four platforms that make up 90% of serious merchant evaluations in 2026. We ranked them on pricing transparency, transaction fees, theme flexibility, app ecosystems, payment gateway choice, SEO capabilities, and scalability for high-volume stores. Each platform has a clear best-fit use case — this ranking helps you pick the right one the first time.</p>
      <p>Also explore our <a href="/reviews/ecommerce/">Ecommerce Pillar</a> for head-to-head comparisons: <a href="/reviews/shopify-vs-woocommerce/">Shopify vs WooCommerce</a>, <a href="/reviews/shopify-vs-bigcommerce/">Shopify vs BigCommerce</a>, and <a href="/reviews/shopify-vs-squarespace/">Shopify vs Squarespace</a>.</p>

      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#how-we-evaluated">How We Evaluated</a></li>
          <li><a href="#ranking-methodology">Ranking Methodology</a></li>
          <li><a href="#quick-comparison">Quick Comparison</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-overall-shopify">#1 — Shopify (Best Overall)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-wordpress-woocommerce">#2 — WooCommerce (Best for WordPress)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-growth-bigcommerce">#3 — BigCommerce (Best for Growth)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#best-design-squarespace">#4 — Squarespace (Best for Design)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#platform-comparison-matrix">Comparison Matrix</a></li>
          <li><a href="#buying-guide">Buying Guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <h2 id="how-we-evaluated">How We Evaluated</h2>
      <p>We evaluated 4 ecommerce platforms based on product documentation, merchant case studies, pricing transparency, feature analysis, and comparison against our <a href="/how-we-test/">ToolStep review protocol</a>. Each platform was assessed across pricing structure, transaction fees, theme and design flexibility, app/extension ecosystem depth, payment gateway choice and fees, built-in SEO capabilities, and scalability for catalogs above 10,000 products and revenue above $1M/year. We did not launch live stores; instead we synthesized the documented experience of merchants in each platform's public forums, help centers, and independent migration guides.</p>

      <h2 id="ranking-methodology">Ranking Methodology</h2>
      <p>Our rankings use weighted scoring across six dimensions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pricing &amp; Fees (25%)</strong> — Subscription cost, transaction fees, payment processing markup, and total cost of ownership at $100k / $500k / $2M annual revenue</li>
        <li><strong>Ease of Launch (20%)</strong> — Onboarding time, number of clicks from signup to first sale, and need for developer assistance</li>
        <li><strong>Themes &amp; Design (15%)</strong> — Free theme quality, premium theme market depth, mobile responsiveness, and visual customization without code</li>
        <li><strong>Apps &amp; Integrations (15%)</strong> — Native features vs apps, marketplace/app store size, and average cost of a functional app stack</li>
        <li><strong>SEO &amp; Marketing (15%)</strong> — URL structure, meta controls, blog/content CMS, sitemaps, structured data, and multi-channel selling (social, POS, marketplace)</li>
        <li><strong>Scalability (10%)</strong> — Performance under load, SKU limits, enterprise migration path, headless/API capability, and support SLAs</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="quick-comparison">Quick Comparison</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Platform</th>
            <th>Best For</th>
            <th>Starting Price</th>
            <th>Transaction Fees</th>
            <th>Rating</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Shopify</strong></td>
            <td>Best Overall</td>
            <td>$39/mo (Basic)</td>
            <td>2.9% + 30¢, 0.5–2% extra on external gateways</td>
            <td>4.7/5</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>WooCommerce</td>
            <td>WordPress / Flexibility</td>
            <td>Free plugin + hosting (~$5–30/mo)</td>
            <td>None by plugin; gateway fees apply</td>
            <td>4.4/5</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>BigCommerce</td>
            <td>Growth &amp; Enterprise</td>
            <td>$39/mo (Standard)</td>
            <td>0% extra on Standard/Plus; gateway only</td>
            <td>4.5/5</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Squarespace</td>
            <td>Design-First Brands</td>
            <td>$23/mo (Basic Commerce)</td>
            <td>2.9% + 30¢ (Basic)</td>
            <td>4.1/5</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
